A version under history/ numbered minor that declares, beneath a struct, a
field the one before it accepted through ...: the immutability violation
keeps the finding at the field, and why declaring it there narrows it.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	meta: {
		owner: string
		...
	}
}
-- ship/history/0.1.thema --
Schema: {
	meta: {
		owner: string
		size?: int
		...
	}
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	meta: {
		owner: string
		size?: int
		...
	}
}
-- out/error --
error[E0207]: immutability violation: v0.1 is not backward compatible with v0.0
 --> history/0.1.thema:1:1
  |
1 | Schema: {
  | ^^^^^^
...
4 |         size?: int
  |         ---- meta.size is now int, which does not accept every value of the prior _
  |
 ::: history/0.0.thema:1:1
  |
1 | Schema: {
  | ------ the version before it
  |
  = note: v0.1 is a minor version, so it must accept all data v0.0 accepts
  = note: v0.0 does not declare meta.size by name, but accepts it through ... or a pattern, so an instance may already hold any value there
  = help: run thema lineage check --published to find which file changed since it was cut, restore it, and make the change in tip.thema
